  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rashid Md Yusuf Shete vs The State Of Maharashtra on 19 June, 2019 Author: Sarang V. Kotwal Bench: Sarang V. Kotwal This Order is modified/corrected by Speaking to Minutes Order dated 10/07/2019 1/3 21-Aba-836- In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.836 Of 2019 Rashid Md Yusuf Shete .... Applicant versus The State of Maharashtra .... Respondent ....... Mr.Veerdhaval Kakade, Advocate for Applicant. Ms.A.A. Takalkar, App for the State/Respondent. Api Shitalkumar Kolhal, Midc Police Station, Solapur, present. Coram : Sarang V. Kotwal, J. Date : 19th June, 2019 P.C. : 1. The Applicant is seeking anticipatory bail in connection with C.R.No.138/18 registered with Midc Police Station, Solapur, under sections 188, 272, 273, 328 r/w 34 of the Indian Penal Code. 2. The FIR is lodged by Food Safety Officer Nasrin Tanvir Mujawar.",
    "facts": "The Applicant is seeking anticipatory bail in connection with C.R.No.138/18 registered with Midc Police Station, Solapur, under sections 188, 272, 273, 328 r/w 34 of the Indian Penal Code. 2. The FIR is lodged by Food Safety Officer Nasrin Tanvir Mujawar. She was informed by the police that on 18/02/2018 at about 06.15 p.m. they had intercepted a vehicle bearing MH-13- AX-1101 and had seized that vehicle. The investigating agency Nesarikar This Order is modified/corrected by Speaking to Minutes Order dated 10/07/2019 2/3 21-ABA-836-19.odt intercepted the vehicle and found out that there were 2 bags (containing 66 packets each) of prohibited substances i.e. Gutkha. All these substances were banned because of notification issued by the Commissioner under the provisions of the Food Safety and Standards Act. The driver of the vehicle was immediately arrested. 3. Further investigation and interrogation of the said driver Jayraj @ Raju Shivmurt Gadgi, revealed that the present Applicant was the owner of the seized articles and therefore he was also arraigned as an accused.",
    "arguments": "Learned Counsel Mr.Kakade submitted that the offence u/s 328 is not made out and that the notification under Food Safety and Standards At, is not issued in accordance with law. He further submitted that unless and until the chemical analysis This Order is modified/corrected by Speaking to Minutes Order dated 10/07/2019 3/3 21-ABA-836-19.odt report is received, no offence as alleged can be said to have been taken place. This contention cannot be accepted at this stage because prima facie, the Food Safety Officer has lodged the FIR mentioning that all these banned substances were seized in the offence. The description of the banned articles is clear enough. 6. The Division Bench of this Court at Aurangabad Bench, in the case of Vasim s/o. Jamil Shaikh Vs. The State of Maharashtra & Anr. in Criminal Application No.4353 of 2016 vide order dated 29/11/2018 has already taken a view that in such cases section 328 of IPC is attracted.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned Counsel Mr.Kakade submitted that the offence u/s 328 is not made out and that the notification under Food Safety and Standards At, is not issued in accordance with law. He further submitted that unless and until the chemical analysis This Order is modified/corrected by Speaking to Minutes Order dated 10/07/2019 3/3 21-ABA-836-19.odt report is received, no offence as alleged can be said to have been taken place. This contention cannot be accepted at this stage because prima facie, the Food Safety Officer has lodged the FIR mentioning that all these banned substances were seized in the offence. The description of the banned articles is clear enough.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "6. The Division Bench of this Court at Aurangabad Bench, in the case of Vasim s/o. Jamil Shaikh Vs. The State of Maharashtra & Anr. in Criminal Application No.4353 of 2016 vide order dated 29/11/2018 has already taken a view that in such cases section 328 of IPC is attracted."
  },
